  "decision_conditions": [
    "Condition : 1 - The development hereby permitted shall be begun before the expiration of three years from the date of this permission.",
    "Condition : 2 - No development shall take place until samples of the materials to be used in the construction of the external surfaces of the hereby permitted have been submitted to and approved in writing by the local planning authority.  Development shall be carried out in accordance with the approved details",
    "Condition : 3 - The proposed development shall be carried out in all respects in accordance with the proposals contained in the application and the plans submitted (Flood Risk Assessment Received: 12 December 2014 5529/S01, 5529/201 Rev. A, 5529/01, 5529/02, 5529/03, 5529/05 Rev. A, 5529/06 Rev. A, 5529/08 Rev. A Received: 15 December 2014 Design and Access Statement, 5529/202 Rev. B, 5529/203 Rev. B, 5529/204 Rev. B, 5529/205 Rev. B, 5529/206 Rev. B, 5529/207 Rev. B, 5529/208 Rev. B, 5529/209 Rev. A, 5529/210 Rev. B Received: 16 December 2014) therewith and approved by the Local Planning Authority, or as shall have been otherwise agreed in writing by the Local Planning Authority before the building is used.",
    "Condition : 4 - No additional windows or other glazed openings shall be formed in the side walls of the extension hereby approved and no additional doors inserted in the building without the prior written consent of the Local Planning Authority.\r\n",
    "Condition : 5 - No demolition or construction work shall take place on the site except between the hours of 8am to 6pm on Mondays to Fridays none shall take place on weekends and public holidays without the prior agreement of the Local Planning Authority.",
    "Condition : 6 - The access doorway to the premises at 35 Turnham Green Terrace shall have a minimum clear width of 900mm, a level surface or ramp between the pavement and the floor and a door handle of not more than 1m above ground level.",
    "Condition : 7 - The rating level of noise emitted from fixed plant on the site, shall be lower than the existing background noise level by 10dB. The noise levels shall be determined at the nearest noise sensitive locations. The measurements shall be made according to BS4142:1997.",
    "Condition : 8 - Deliveries and servicing associated with the commercial unit shall only be carried out between the following hours, Monday to Saturday 07:00 - 23:00 and Sunday 09:00 - 22:00."
  ],
